.TH G15CTL 1 "2026" "g15ctl 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
g15ctl \- fan and thermal control for Dell G\-series laptops
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B g15ctl
.RI [ options ]
.IR command " [" args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B g15ctl
controls fan speed, thermal profiles and G\-Mode on Dell G\-series laptops by
driving the same AWCC firmware interface that Alienware Command Center uses on
Windows.
.PP
Reading sensors works as an unprivileged user. Changing thermal state requires
root.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show thermal mode, fan speeds, temperatures and battery health. Accepts
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.B monitor
Live terminal dashboard with a temperature trend sparkline. Press
.B q
to quit; number keys switch mode when run as root.
.TP
.BI mode " [name]"
Print the current mode, or set it. With no argument, lists what the firmware
supports. Typical names are
.BR quiet ,
.BR balanced ,
.BR balanced\-performance ,
.B low\-power
and
.BR g\-mode .
Aliases such as
.BR perf ,
.B silent
and
.B turbo
are accepted.
.TP
.BI fan " [percent|auto]"
Set a manual fan boost from 0 to 100, or
.B auto
to hand the fans back to the firmware. See
.B FAN BOOST SEMANTICS
below.
.TP
.BI gmode " [on|off|toggle|status]"
Control G\-Mode, the maximum\-performance mode bound to the keyboard's G key on
Windows.
.TP
.BI curve " [show|set|enable|disable]"
Inspect or edit the automatic fan curve. Points are given as
.IR TEMP : PERCENT
pairs, for example
.RB ` "g15ctl curve set 50:0 70:35 85:100" '.
The curve is applied by the background service.
.TP
.B reset
Return all thermal control to the firmware: clears fan boost, disables G\-Mode
and selects the default profile.
.TP
.B restore
Reapply the last saved mode. Used by the boot and resume units.
.TP
.B doctor
Diagnose hardware support, list available backends and warn about other
daemons that might contend for thermal control.
.TP
.B logs
Show service logs from the journal and
.IR /var/log/g15ctl/g15ctl.log .
Accepts
.B \-n
and
.BR \-f .
.TP
.B daemon
Run the background service. Normally started via systemd, not by hand.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-backend " name"
Force a backend:
.BR awcc\-acpi ,
.B awcc\-native
or
.BR dell\-pc .
By default the most capable available backend is chosen.
.TP
.BR \-v , " \-\-verbose"
Debug logging.
.TP
.BR \-q , " \-\-quiet"
Warnings and errors only.
.SH FAN BOOST SEMANTICS
The firmware does not accept an absolute fan PWM. It accepts a
.I boost
value from 0 to 255 which raises the floor of the firmware's own fan curve,
approximately
.PP
.RS
pwm = pwm_base + (boost / 255) * (pwm_max \- pwm_base)
.RE
.PP
So
.B g15ctl fan 50
guarantees the fan runs at least around half speed; the firmware will still
spin it faster if it decides more cooling is needed. This is why a boost can
never make the machine run hotter than leaving it on automatic.
.SH BACKENDS
.TP
.B awcc\-acpi
Calls the firmware's WMAX method through
.IR /proc/acpi/call .
The only backend supporting thermal profiles, G\-Mode and per\-fan boost
together. Requires the
.B acpi_call
module and root.
.TP
.B awcc\-native
The in\-tree
.B alienware\-wmi
driver loaded with
.BR force_platform_profile=1 .
Provides profiles and G\-Mode. Manual fan control additionally needs kernel
6.15 or newer with
.BR force_hwmon=1 .
.TP
.B dell\-pc
The generic Dell SMBIOS thermal driver. Profiles only. Always present, so
.B g15ctl
degrades rather than failing.
.SH DUAL BOOT
Fan boost and G\-Mode are volatile EC state, but survive a warm reboot.
.B g15ctl
therefore clears them on shutdown via
.BR g15ctl\-reset.service ,
so a reboot into Windows always hands Alienware Command Center the firmware
default. Nothing is written to BIOS NVRAM.
.SH SAFETY
A watchdog in the background service monitors the hottest relevant sensor.
Above 88 C it forces the fans to maximum regardless of the requested speed;
above 95 C it releases control to the firmware entirely, on the grounds that
the firmware's curve is thermally validated and a user\-space curve is not.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/g15ctl/config.json
Policy: default mode, watchdog thresholds, fan curve.
.TP
.I /var/lib/g15ctl/state.json
Last applied mode, used by
.BR restore .
.TP
.I /var/log/g15ctl/g15ctl.log
Rotating log file.
.TP
.I /etc/modprobe.d/g15ctl.conf
Module parameters enabling the native AWCC driver.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on error, 130 if interrupted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Quiet the machine down:
.B sudo g15ctl mode quiet
.TP
Pin the fans at 70% before a long compile:
.B sudo g15ctl fan 70
.TP
Hand the fans back to the firmware:
.B sudo g15ctl fan auto
.TP
Watch what is happening:
.B g15ctl monitor
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sensors (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR powerprofilesctl (1)
.PP
Kernel documentation:
.I Documentation/admin-guide/laptops/alienware-wmi.rst
.SH AUTHORS
Developed and verified against a Dell G15 5530, BIOS 1.34.0, by reading the
machine's own ACPI tables rather than porting constants from other models.
